 ### Local Sampling
-Uses depth information to guide sampling along the ray, reducing the number of samples and replacing the coarse NeRF network [S1].
+Uses depth information to guide sampling along the ray, reducing the number of samples and replacing the coarse NeRF network [S1]. It is chosen when dense depth priors are available to accelerate convergence and improve geometry [S1].
 
 ### Depth Uncertainty Modeling
-Incorporates depth uncertainty into a multivariate Gaussian method to query the MLP, allowing the network to learn multiple scales of uncertainty [S1].
+Incorporates depth uncertainty into a multivariate Gaussian method to query the MLP, allowing the network to learn multiple scales of uncertainty [S1]. It is chosen when depth measurements have varying reliability, as it normalizes the geometric loss by variance [S1].
 
 ### Joint Loss Optimization
-Minimizes a joint loss function combining photometric (L1 color difference) and geometric (L1 depth difference normalized by variance) losses [S1].
+Minimizes a joint loss function combining photometric (L1 color difference) and geometric (L1 depth difference normalized by variance) losses [S1]. It is chosen when simultaneous photometric and geometric accuracy is required, particularly with limited input views [S1].
 
